**Gates before launch**

I run four gates in order before I launch the script. First, I check that spe/predictions/r04.yaml and spe/plans/r04.md are in a commit that comes before any harness or trial work. Second, I run the grader selftest. grade.py must pass the oracle labels from answers.json and fail both an empty label file and a file of wrong labels. judge.md must also score a known polite reply above a known rude one. Third, I regrade round 3's saved results with this round's grade.py and judge. If any score differs from what round 3 recorded, that is a grader change, and I report it before going on. Fourth, I do a dry run on 3 cells with args.only and args.spendCapUsd set to 2. I check four things in that run: every result fits its schema, the leak scan is clean, no staged ticket has a label field, and both configs pass the prompt-length and tool-count checks. When all four gates pass, I commit "SPE r04 evaluate (harness): ..." and start the full run. My cost estimate of about $30 is unmeasured.

**Things I had to make into arguments.** I could not read r03-workflow.js, so I don't know how it started a config on a ticket or how it called grade.py. You pass the run command in as `args.runnerCmd`. The config and ticket file paths come in as `args.configSource` and `args.ticketSource`. The grade agent copies the grade.py command from the previous round's script. The per-call cost defaults are placeholders. Set them from r03's measured costs.

**spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js**

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-evaluate-support-configs',
  description: 'SPE evaluate. Runs configs B and C2 on the support tickets, grades labels with grade.py, judges reply tone with Opus, and stops at the spend cap.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Setup' },
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Leak scan' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Judge' },
    { title: 'Top-up' },
    { title: 'Synthesis' },
  ],
}

// ---------- Arguments ----------
const A = args && typeof args === 'object' ? args : {}
const ROUND = A.round ?? 4
const RR = String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0')
const PREV = String(ROUND - 1).padStart(2, '0')
const CONFIGS = A.configs ?? ['B', 'C2']
const CONFIG_SRC = A.configSource ?? {}
const EXPECT = A.expect ?? {
  B: { promptLines: 12, toolCount: 6, mustHaveTools: [] },
  C2: { promptLines: 12, toolCount: 4, mustHaveTools: ['check_status'] },
}
const TICKET_SRC = A.ticketSource ?? 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets.json'
const TICKET_COUNT = A.ticketCount ?? 50
const TRIALS = A.trialsPerCell ?? 5
const TOPUP_MAX = A.topUpMax ?? 5
const CAP = A.spendCapUsd ?? 40
const EST = {
  trial: A.estTrialUsd ?? 0.03,
  judge: A.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.02,
  fixed: A.estFixedUsd ?? 3,
}
const BATCH = A.batchSize ?? 20
const TRIAL_MODEL = A.trialModel ?? 'opus'
const JUDGE_MODEL = 'opus'
const RUNNER = A.runnerCmd
const ONLY = Array.isArray(A.only) ? A.only : null
const DRY = ONLY !== null
const WORK = `/tmp/spe-r${RR}${DRY ? '-dry' : ''}`
const OUT = `spe/evals/results/r${RR}${DRY ? '-dry' : ''}`

// ---------- Budget and halt ----------
let spent = EST.fixed
let halted = null // { kind: 'budget' | 'integrity', reason }
const skipped = []

function halt(kind, reason) {
  if (!halted) {
    halted = { kind, reason }
    log(`HALT (${kind}): ${reason}`)
  }
}

function reserve(kind, id, est) {
  if (halted) {
    skipped.push({ kind, id, reason: halted.reason })
    return false
  }
  if (spent + est > CAP) {
    halt('budget', `spend cap $${CAP} would be crossed at an estimated $${spent.toFixed(2)}`)
    skipped.push({ kind, id, reason: halted.reason })
    return false
  }
  spent += est
  return true
}

function settle(est, actual) {
  if (typeof actual === 'number' && actual >= 0) spent += actual - est
}

// ---------- Schemas ----------
const SETUP_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    ticketIds: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    configs: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          name: { type: 'string' },
          promptLines: { type: 'integer' },
          toolNames: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        },
        required: ['name', 'promptLines', 'toolNames'],
      },
    },
    fieldsStripped: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    labelFieldsFoundInStage: { type: 'boolean' },
    notes: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
  },
  required: ['ticketIds', 'configs', 'fieldsStripped', 'labelFieldsFoundInStage'],
}

const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    status: { type: 'string', enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
    label: {
      type: ['object', 'null'],
      properties: {
        category: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
        priority: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
      },
    },
    reply: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
    toolCalls: { type: 'integer' },
    toolCallsByName: { type: 'object', additionalProperties: { type: 'integer' } },
    toolErrors: { type: 'integer' },
    inputTokens: { type: 'integer' },
    outputTokens: { type: 'integer' },
    runtimeSec: { type: 'number' },
    costUsd: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
    pathsRead: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
  },
  required: ['status', 'label', 'reply', 'toolCalls', 'toolErrors', 'inputTokens', 'outputTokens', 'runtimeSec', 'pathsRead'],
}

const LEAK_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    scannedCount: { type: 'integer' },
    leakedIds: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    evidence: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: { trialId: { type: 'string' }, path: { type: 'string' } },
        required: ['trialId', 'path'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['scannedCount', 'leakedIds', 'evidence'],
}

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    graderBroken: { type: 'boolean' },
    error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
    rows: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          trialId: { type: 'string' },
          categoryOk: { type: 'boolean' },
          priorityOk: { type: 'boolean' },
          graderError: { type: 'boolean' },
        },
        required: ['trialId', 'categoryOk', 'priorityOk', 'graderError'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['graderBroken', 'rows'],
}

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    score: { type: 'number' },
    pass: { type: 'boolean' },
    reason: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['score', 'pass', 'reason'],
}

const ANALYSIS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    clusters: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          id: { type: 'string' },
          cause: { type: 'string' },
          configs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          ticketIds: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          count: { type: 'integer' },
          example: { type: 'string' },
          newThisRound: { type: 'boolean' },
        },
        required: ['id', 'cause', 'configs', 'ticketIds', 'count', 'newThisRound'],
      },
    },
    notes: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
  },
  required: ['clusters'],
}

const COMPARE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    rows: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          metric: { type: 'string' },
          config: { type: 'string' },
          predicted: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          statedError: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          measured: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          withinError: { type: ['boolean', 'null'] },
          graderCheck: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['metric', 'config', 'predicted', 'measured', 'withinError'],
      },
    },
    unmeasuredPredictions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
  required: ['rows', 'unmeasuredPredictions'],
}

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
  required: ['complete', 'gaps'],
}

// ---------- Helpers ----------
const cellKey = t => `${t.cfg}:${t.ticket}`
const passed = t => t.status === 'completed' && t.categoryOk === true && t.priorityOk === true

async function runBatched(items, fn, label) {
  const out = []
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += BATCH) {
    const chunk = items.slice(i, i + BATCH)
    const res = await parallel(chunk.map(s => () => fn(s)))
    out.push(...res)
    log(`${label}: ${Math.min(i + BATCH, items.length)}/${items.length} done, estimated spend $${spent.toFixed(2)} of $${CAP}`)
  }
  return out
}

function trialPrompt(s) {
  return `You run one trial of an evaluation. Trial id: ${s.id}.

Run this command once from the repository root and wait for it to finish:
${RUNNER} --config ${WORK}/configs/${s.cfg} --ticket ${WORK}/tickets/${s.ticket}.json

Read rules. You may read only files under ${WORK}/configs/${s.cfg}/ and the file ${WORK}/tickets/${s.ticket}.json. Do not open, list, grep, or cat any path under spe/. Do not look for answers, graders, plans, or predictions. Do not change, fix, or retry the answer the command produced.

Copy the command's output into the result fields. Status rules:
- "completed" means the command finished. A wrong, empty, or malformed label is still "completed". Put a null label in that case.
- "harness_error" means the command itself crashed or could not start.
- "rate_limited" means the command hit a rate limit.
List in pathsRead every file you opened.`
}

async function runTrial(s) {
  if (!reserve('trial', s.id, EST.trial)) return { ...s, status: 'skipped' }
  let r
  try {
    r = await agent(trialPrompt(s), {
      label: `trial ${s.id}`,
      phase: s.primary ? 'Trials' : 'Top-up',
      schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
      model: TRIAL_MODEL,
    })
  } catch (e) {
    return { ...s, status: 'harness_error', error: String(e) }
  }
  settle(EST.trial, r?.costUsd)
  return { ...s, ...r, status: r?.status ?? 'harness_error' }
}

async function leakScan(trials, ph) {
  const done = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed')
  if (!done.length) return []
  const voided = new Set()
  for (const t of done) {
    if ((t.pathsRead || []).some(p => p.includes('spe/'))) voided.add(t.id)
  }
  if (A.transcriptDir) {
    const r = await agent(
      `Scan agent transcripts under ${A.transcriptDir}. Look only at agents whose label is one of these:
${done.map(t => `trial ${t.id}`).join('\n')}

For each one, find any tool call that reads, lists, greps, globs, or cats a path containing spe/evals/, spe/predictions/, spe/plans/, answers.json, grade.py, or judge.md. Report the trial ids that did, with the path as evidence. Report nothing else.`,
      { label: `leak scan ${ph}`, phase: 'Leak scan', schema: LEAK_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
    )
    for (const id of r?.leakedIds || []) voided.add(id)
    if (!r || r.scannedCount < done.length) {
      log(`Leak scan covered ${r?.scannedCount ?? 0} of ${done.length} trials. Treat the uncovered trials as unscanned.`)
    }
  } else {
    log('No args.transcriptDir. The leak scan used self-reported paths only. That is a weaker check.')
  }
  for (const t of trials) if (voided.has(t.id)) t.status = 'voided'
  if (voided.size) halt('integrity', `answer-key leak: ${[...voided].join(', ')}`)
  return [...voided]
}

async function gradeAll(trials, tag) {
  if (halted?.kind === 'integrity') return
  for (const cfg of CONFIGS) {
    const group = trials.filter(t => t.cfg === cfg && t.status === 'completed')
    if (!group.length) continue
    const lines = group
      .map(t => JSON.stringify({ trial_id: t.id, ticket_id: t.ticket, label: t.label ?? null }))
      .join('\n')
    const r = await agent(
      `Grade trial labels with the code grader. Do not judge anything yourself.

1. Write these lines exactly as given to ${OUT}/labels-${cfg}-${tag}.jsonl:
${lines}

2. Run spe/evals/graders/grade.py on that file against spe/evals/tasks/answers.json. Use the same command form as spe/evals/harness/r${PREV}-workflow.js. Save its output to ${OUT}/grades-${cfg}-${tag}.jsonl.

3. Return one row per trial id with categoryOk and priorityOk exactly as grade.py reported them. If grade.py errors on one row, set graderError true for that row. If grade.py fails as a whole, set graderBroken true, put the error text in error, and stop.`,
      { label: `grade ${cfg} ${tag}`, phase: 'Grade', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
    )
    if (!r || r.graderBroken) {
      halt('integrity', `grade.py broke on ${cfg} ${tag}: ${r?.error ?? 'no result'}`)
      return
    }
    const byId = new Map(r.rows.map(x => [x.trialId, x]))
    let bad = 0
    for (const t of group) {
      const g = byId.get(t.id)
      if (!g || g.graderError) {
        t.status = 'grader_error'
        bad++
        continue
      }
      t.categoryOk = g.categoryOk
      t.priorityOk = g.priorityOk
    }
    if (bad) {
      halt('integrity', `grade.py returned no usable row for ${bad} ${cfg} trials in ${tag}`)
      return
    }
  }
}

async function judgeOne(t) {
  if (!reserve('judge', t.id, EST.judge)) return t
  const r = await agent(
    `You grade the tone of one support reply. Read the rubric in spe/evals/graders/judge.md and follow it exactly.

The customer ticket is in ${WORK}/tickets/${t.ticket}.json.
The reply to grade is between the markers.
<<<REPLY
${t.reply ?? ''}
REPLY>>>

Grade only tone as the rubric defines it. Do not grade the label or the facts. You are not told which configuration wrote this reply. Do not try to guess it.`,
    { label: `judge ${t.ticket} #${t.judgeIdx}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL },
  )
  t.tone = r ?? null
  return t
}

async function judgeAll(trials) {
  if (halted?.kind === 'integrity') return
  const todo = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.tone)
  todo.forEach((t, i) => { t.judgeIdx = i + 1 })
  await runBatched(todo, judgeOne, 'Judge')
}

function stats(list) {
  const done = list.filter(t => t.status === 'completed')
  const judged = done.filter(t => t.tone)
  const n = done.length
  const mean = f => (n ? done.reduce((a, t) => a + (Number(t[f]) || 0), 0) / n : null)
  const rate = (arr, pred) => (arr.length ? arr.filter(pred).length / arr.length : null)
  return {
    attempted: list.length,
    completed: n,
    harnessErrors: list.filter(t => t.status === 'harness_error').length,
    rateLimited: list.filter(t => t.status === 'rate_limited').length,
    voided: list.filter(t => t.status === 'voided').length,
    graderErrors: list.filter(t => t.status === 'grader_error').length,
    skipped: list.filter(t => t.status === 'skipped').length,
    passRate: rate(done, passed),
    categoryAcc: rate(done, t => t.categoryOk === true),
    priorityAcc: rate(done, t => t.priorityOk === true),
    judged: judged.length,
    tonePassRate: rate(judged, t => t.tone.pass === true),
    meanToneScore: judged.length ? judged.reduce((a, t) => a + t.tone.score, 0) / judged.length : null,
    meanToolCalls: mean('toolCalls'),
    meanToolErrors: mean('toolErrors'),
    meanInputTokens: mean('inputTokens'),
    meanOutputTokens: mean('outputTokens'),
    meanRuntimeSec: mean('runtimeSec'),
    meanCostUsd: mean('costUsd'),
    checkStatusCallsPerTrial: n
      ? done.reduce((a, t) => a + ((t.toolCallsByName || {}).check_status || 0), 0) / n
      : null,
  }
}

// ---------- Main ----------
async function main() {
  if (!RUNNER) {
    log(`Missing args.runnerCmd. Copy the trial command from spe/evals/harness/r${PREV}-workflow.js and pass it in.`)
    return { ok: false, reason: 'missing args.runnerCmd' }
  }
  log(`Round ${ROUND}${DRY ? ' DRY RUN' : ''}. Configs ${CONFIGS.join(', ')}. ${TRIALS} trials per cell. Cap $${CAP}. Spend figures are estimates until trials report costUsd.`)

  // Setup
  phase('Setup')
  const setup = await agent(
    `Stage inputs for an evaluation round. You are not a trial.

1. Read the tickets from ${TICKET_SRC}. If that file does not exist, use the ticket file under spe/evals/tasks/ that is not answers.json. For each ticket write ${WORK}/tickets/<ticket_id>.json with only the fields a support agent would see. Remove every field that holds a label, category, priority, answer, or expected value. Do not copy spe/evals/tasks/answers.json or anything under spe/evals/graders/.

2. For each config in [${CONFIGS.join(', ')}], copy its system prompt and tool definitions to ${WORK}/configs/<config>/. Source paths: ${JSON.stringify(CONFIG_SRC)}. If a source is not listed, find it from spe/plans/r${RR}.md and spe/evals/harness/r${PREV}-workflow.js. Report each config's prompt line count and tool names.

3. Check every staged ticket file for a category or priority key. Set labelFieldsFoundInStage to true if any remain.

Return the ticket ids in sorted order.`,
    { label: 'setup', phase: 'Setup', schema: SETUP_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
  )
  if (!setup) return { ok: false, reason: 'setup returned nothing' }
  if (setup.labelFieldsFoundInStage) {
    halt('integrity', 'label fields survived in the staged tickets')
    return { ok: false, halted }
  }
  if (setup.ticketIds.length !== TICKET_COUNT) {
    log(`Setup found ${setup.ticketIds.length} tickets. The plan says ${TICKET_COUNT}. Stopping.`)
    return { ok: false, reason: 'ticket count mismatch', found: setup.ticketIds.length }
  }
  for (const cfg of CONFIGS) {
    const got = setup.configs.find(c => c.name === cfg)
    const want = EXPECT[cfg]
    if (!got) return { ok: false, reason: `config ${cfg} not staged` }
    if (want) {
      const missing = want.mustHaveTools.filter(x => !got.toolNames.includes(x))
      if (got.promptLines !== want.promptLines || got.toolNames.length !== want.toolCount || missing.length) {
        log(`Config ${cfg} does not match the plan. Prompt lines ${got.promptLines}, tools [${got.toolNames.join(', ')}]. Stopping.`)
        return { ok: false, reason: `config ${cfg} mismatch`, got }
      }
    }
  }

  // Trials
  phase('Trials')
  const specs = []
  for (const cfg of CONFIGS) {
    for (const ticket of setup.ticketIds) {
      if (ONLY && !ONLY.includes(`${cfg}:${ticket}`)) continue
      for (let k = 1; k <= TRIALS; k++) {
        specs.push({ id: `${cfg}:${ticket}:t${k}`, cfg, ticket, primary: true })
      }
    }
  }
  log(`${specs.length} primary trials queued.`)
  const trials = await runBatched(specs, runTrial, 'Trials')

  // Leak scan
  phase('Leak scan')
  const voided = await leakScan(trials, 'primary')

  // Grade
  phase('Grade')
  await gradeAll(trials, 'primary')

  // Judge
  phase('Judge')
  log('The tone judge is Opus, the same model family as the trials. No judge from another family is available, so tone scores may share blind spots with the agent under test.')
  await judgeAll(trials)

  // Top-up
  phase('Top-up')
  const cells = new Map()
  for (const t of trials) {
    const key = cellKey(t)
    if (!cells.has(key)) cells.set(key, [])
    cells.get(key).push(t)
  }
  const mixed = [...cells.entries()]
    .filter(([, ts]) => {
      const done = ts.filter(t => t.status === 'completed')
      const p = done.filter(passed).length
      return done.length > 0 && p > 0 && p < done.length
    })
    .map(([key]) => key)
  let topups = []
  if (halted) {
    log(`Top-up skipped because the round halted: ${halted.reason}`)
  } else if (mixed.length) {
    const topSpecs = []
    for (const key of mixed) {
      const [cfg, ticket] = key.split(':')
      for (let k = TRIALS + 1; k <= TRIALS + TOPUP_MAX; k++) {
        topSpecs.push({ id: `${cfg}:${ticket}:t${k}`, cfg, ticket, primary: false })
      }
    }
    log(`${mixed.length} mixed cells get up to ${TOPUP_MAX} extra trials each (${topSpecs.length} total).`)
    topups = await runBatched(topSpecs, runTrial, 'Top-up')
    voided.push(...(await leakScan(topups, 'top-up')))
    await gradeAll(topups, 'topup')
    await judgeAll(topups)
  } else {
    log('No mixed cells. No top-up trials.')
  }

  // Synthesis
  phase('Synthesis')
  const all = [...trials, ...topups]
  const primary = all.filter(t => t.primary)
  const perConfig = {}
  for (const cfg of CONFIGS) {
    perConfig[cfg] = {
      headline: stats(primary.filter(t => t.cfg === cfg)),
      allTrials: stats(all.filter(t => t.cfg === cfg)),
    }
  }
  const perCell = {}
  for (const t of all) {
    const key = cellKey(t)
    if (!perCell[key]) perCell[key] = { completed: 0, passed: 0, tonePassed: 0, judged: 0 }
    if (t.status === 'completed') {
      perCell[key].completed++
      if (passed(t)) perCell[key].passed++
      if (t.tone) {
        perCell[key].judged++
        if (t.tone.pass) perCell[key].tonePassed++
      }
    }
  }
  const summary = {
    round: ROUND,
    dry: DRY,
    halted,
    spendEstimateUsd: Number(spent.toFixed(2)),
    capUsd: CAP,
    perConfig,
    mixedCells: mixed,
    voided,
    skipped,
    note: 'Headline stats use primary trials only. Top-up trials feed per-cell pass rates. Harness errors, rate limits, voided trials, and grader errors are not counted as model failures.',
  }

  await agent(
    `Write evaluation results to disk. Do not change any numbers.
1. Write this JSON to ${OUT}/summary.json:
${JSON.stringify(summary)}
2. Write one JSON line per trial to ${OUT}/trials.jsonl from this array:
${JSON.stringify(all)}
3. Write this per-cell table to ${OUT}/cells.json:
${JSON.stringify(perCell)}`,
    { label: 'write results', phase: 'Synthesis', model: 'opus' },
  )

  const failed = all.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && (!passed(t) || (t.tone && !t.tone.pass)))
  const [analysis, compare] = await parallel([
    () => agent(
      `You do failure analysis for one evaluation round. These trials failed the label grader, the tone judge, or both:
${JSON.stringify(failed.map(t => ({ id: t.id, cfg: t.cfg, ticket: t.ticket, label: t.label, categoryOk: t.categoryOk, priorityOk: t.priorityOk, tone: t.tone, reply: t.reply, toolCallsByName: t.toolCallsByName, toolErrors: t.toolErrors })))}

You may read spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, the staged tickets in ${WORK}/tickets/, and spe/failures.md. Group the failures by cause. Give each new cluster an id like F-r${RR}-01. Mark clusters that match an existing entry in spe/failures.md as not new and use that entry's id. Say which config each cluster hits. Write your analysis to ${OUT}/failure-analysis.md. Do not edit spe/failures.md.`,
      { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: ANALYSIS_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
    ),
    () => agent(
      `Compare measured results to the saved predictions. Read spe/predictions/r${RR}.yaml. Measured results per config:
${JSON.stringify(perConfig)}

For every predicted number, give the measured value, the stated error, and whether the measured value is within it. Name the grader check that measured it. List any prediction that has no measured value. Write the table to ${OUT}/vs-predictions.md. Do not edit spe/prediction-log.md.`,
      { label: 'compare to predictions', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: COMPARE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
    ),
  ])

  const critic = await agent(
    `You check one evaluation round for completeness. Do not rerun anything.
Plan: configs ${CONFIGS.join(', ')}, ${TICKET_COUNT} tickets, ${TRIALS} trials per cell, code grader on label.category and label.priority, Opus tone judge, cap $${CAP}${DRY ? ', dry run limited to ' + ONLY.join(', ') : ''}.
Summary: ${JSON.stringify(summary)}
Per-cell table: ${JSON.stringify(perCell)}
Prediction comparison: ${JSON.stringify(compare)}
Failure clusters: ${JSON.stringify(analysis?.clusters ?? [])}

